The entire method will be rewritten to implement a strict, state-machine-based parser. The core of the security fix is to add a new state, `"chunk_terminator"`, which explicitly reads the two bytes following a data chunk and validates that they are exactly `b"\r\n"`. If the terminator is incorrect, an error is raised, thus preventing the smuggling vulnerability. The refactoring also improves the overall clarity and correctness of the chunked-body parsing logic, though it introduces a documented behavioral change of emitting an empty `Data` event to signal the start of a new chunk.

